    <section id="faq" class="band"><div class="inner"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23q1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#q1">What does this collection mesh together?</a></summary><p>It links Visual Capitalist country, group, and confederation coverage with The Guardian player-guide metadata for the same 2026 World Cup field.</p></details>
<details><summary><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23q2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#q2">Why model teams separately from source articles?</a></summary><p>Teams are reusable tournament entities, while the two articles are provenance-bearing CreativeWork entities that contribute different layers of evidence.</p></details>
<details><summary><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23q3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#q3">Why are all 1,248 players not duplicated here?</a></summary><p>The Guardian source is represented as the authoritative player-guide layer; this collection indexes that layer without reproducing every profile.</p></details>
<details><summary><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23q4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#q4">Why include a bracket section before results are known?</a></summary><p>The bracket section models advancement rules and round placeholders, not predicted winners, so it adds tournament-path structure without inventing outcomes.</p></details>
<details><summary><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23q5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#q5">What is the main analytical value?</a></summary><p>Users can move from groups and confederations to the player-guide source and then into the possible route from Round of 32 to the final.</p></details>
<details><summary><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23q6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#q6">How can this RDF be extended?</a></summary><p>Add squad-member entities from a licensed or locally extracted player dataset, then connect each player to a team, role, club, and Guardian profile card identifier.</p></details><h2 style="margin-top:30px">Glossary</h2><div class="glossary"><article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23qualified-team" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#qualified-team">Qualified team</a></h3><p>A national team listed as part of the 48-country 2026 FIFA World Cup field.</p></article>
<article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23group-stage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#group-stage">Group stage</a></h3><p>The opening tournament phase, modeled here as 12 groups of four teams.</p></article>
<article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23round-of-32" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#round-of-32">Round of 32</a></h3><p>The first knockout round, reached by the top two teams in each group and the eight best third-place teams.</p></article>
<article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23knockout-path" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#knockout-path">Knockout path</a></h3><p>The single-elimination route from Round of 32 through Round of 16, quarter-finals, semi-finals, and final.</p></article>
<article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23confederation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#confederation">Confederation</a></h3><p>A regional football governing body such as UEFA, CAF, AFC, CONCACAF, CONMEBOL, or OFC.</p></article>
<article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23player-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#player-guide">Player guide</a></h3><p>A source work that profiles squad members and supplies micro-level context about a tournament field.</p></article>
<article><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23semantic-meshup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#semantic-meshup">Semantic meshup</a></h3><p>A fusion of multiple sources using RDF entities, typed relationships, and resolver-backed identifiers.</p></article></div><h2 style="margin-top:30px">How To Extend</h2><div class="howto"><article class="step"><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23step1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#step1">Start with country participation</a></h3><p>Model each qualified national team with group and confederation facts so the tournament field has a stable macro-level index.</p></article>
<article class="step"><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23step2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#step2">Attach source provenance</a></h3><p>Represent each source article as a CreativeWork and link the claims or datasets it supports back to that source.</p></article>
<article class="step"><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23step3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#step3">Connect player coverage to teams</a></h3><p>Use The Guardian player guide as the player-layer source and connect its coverage to the same teams modeled from the country table.</p></article>
<article class="step"><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23step4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#step4">Model the bracket as slots, not predictions</a></h3><p>Represent advancement rules and knockout rounds with placeholders until results determine actual team paths.</p></article>
<article class="step"><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23step5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#step5">Keep source scopes distinct</a></h3><p>Do not collapse Visual Capitalist country-list facts, Guardian player-guide metadata, and FIFA format rules into one undifferentiated article entity.</p></article>
<article class="step"><h3><a class="entity-link" href="https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.visualcapitalist.com%2Fevery-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup%2F%23step6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-iri="https://www.visualcapitalist.com/every-country-playing-in-the-2026-world-cup/#step6">Publish resolver-backed companions</a></h3><p>Expose both RDF and HTML with links that let readers inspect every entity through a Linked Data resolver.</p></article></div></div></section>
